// `sales` passes a sack count to `pantry.take_flour`, so `SackCount` is
// used by two domains and lives here. The compiler asks for that move
// (`layout.promotion_required`) the moment a second domain uses a type,
// with a one-step fix; it never moves code back on its own.

/// How many 16-kilogram sacks of flour the pantry holds.
type SackCount = Int {
    min: 0
    max: 6
}
